  "label": "Gorgias",
  "description": "Read support tickets, messages, and customers, and update ticket status, priority, and tags.",
  "securityDescription": "Gorgias sign-in opens through Composio, which asks for the helpdesk's Gorgias subdomain. Agents act as the signed-in Gorgias user and can read tickets, messages, customers, tags, views, custom field values, teams, and helpdesk users. With write access, Agents can change a ticket's status, subject, priority, and language, add and remove ticket tags, and create customers and edit their names. Closing a ticket can send the customer a satisfaction survey when the helpdesk has surveys turned on, and the helpdesk's rules can act on these changes, as they do for changes people make. Agents cannot reply to customers or send any message, create tickets, add internal notes, assign tickets, move a ticket to another customer, set or change a customer's email addresses or phone numbers, delete or merge anything, or change rules, macros, views, teams, users, integrations, or account settings.",
